  "body": "Follow-up to #261 / PR #861 (a refused generation shows the moves it had built as a dashed ghost).\n\nPR #861 gives a ghost to the refusals that fire on a finished path (the not-centre-cutting refusal in Pocket, Adaptive2D, Offset2D, Contour, both Slot kinds, Bore, Circular and the 3D ladder; the plunge checks on the 3D finish and multiaxis guards, Rotary Offset's bar check, the posed check and the facer's air-entry fallback). `docs/decisions/261-refusal-ghost.md` lists what still carries none:\n\n- generators that refuse part-way, before their path is finished - getting the partial path out means restructuring their control flow;\n- Rotary Offset's inner ladder, which drops its ghost on purpose because those moves are in unwrapped coordinates, not where the part is;\n- anything that refuses before building a move (parameter, region and tool checks, drilling, the bore and thread-mill hole checks) - nothing to show, not owed.\n\nAlso from the review of #861:\n- `crates/app/src/operation/cross_spindle.rs` (`in_world`, about lines 182-199) and `crates/app/src/operation/picks.rs` (`door_refusal`, about 117-120) do not handle the `Ghosted` variant specifically; unreachable today, but a ghost-carrying refusal routed through them would keep its message and spot unrewritten.\n- The ghost's colour darkens toward black instead of using the ground-aware dimming from #698, so it has no light-ground contrast test.\n\nDone means: each generator that can refuse part-way either hands back its partial path (in world coordinates) or is listed as \"nothing useful to show\" with the reason; the two match sites handle the ghost variant; the ghost reads on the light ground, pinned by the contrast test. No generator's successful output changes (goldens byte-identical).\n\nEffort is `high` because it touches generator code (safety floor), although the change is display-only.\n",
